---
/**
 * D1. /guides/free-manhwa-official-apps — the most popular manhwa with a
 * free official option, by the same rule as the /<kind>/<slug>/free pages
 * (freeSplit in answers.mjs). Counted from the catalog on every build.
 */
export const prerender = true
import DataGuide from '../../components/DataGuide.astro'
import DataList from '../../components/DataList.astro'
import { comicsOfCountry, hubSlugOf } from '../../lib/catalog.js'
import { pathOfTitle } from '../../lib/section.mjs'
import { noindexSubpages } from '../../lib/thin-pages.mjs'
import { indexKeepOnce } from '../../lib/index-keep.js'
import { factsFor } from '../../lib/platform-facts.js'
import { dataGuide } from '../../lib/guides-registry.js'
import { freeRows, countPlatforms, platformLabel, notAdult, thumbOf, factLine, num, percent, listWords } from '../../lib/data-guides.mjs'
import homeRules from '../../../data/home-rules.json'

const slug = 'free-manhwa-official-apps'
const meta = dataGuide(slug)
const LIST_SIZE = 50

const manhwa = comicsOfCountry('KR')
const keep = notAdult(homeRules)
const everyFree = freeRows(manhwa, { limit: Infinity, keep })
const rows = everyFree.slice(0, LIST_SIZE)
const withLinks = manhwa.filter((m) => (m.readLinks || []).length > 0 && keep(m)).length
const platforms = countPlatforms(rows)
const top = rows[0]?.item
const englishFree = everyFree.filter((r) => r.english).length

// The unique banner npm run guides:media assigned this guide (src/lib/guides.mjs assignBanners).
const hero = meta.image ? { src: meta.image, alt: meta.imageAlt || meta.title, wide: meta.wide } : null
const list = rows.map(({ item, free }) => ({
  title: item.title,
  path: pathOfTitle(item),
  cover: thumbOf(item.cover),
  sub: factLine(item),
  platforms: free.map(platformLabel).join(', '),
  // A noindexed /free page stays live but is not linked from the guide.
  extra: noindexSubpages(item, indexKeepOnce()).includes('free')
    ? null
    : { href: `${pathOfTitle(item)}/free`, text: `How to read ${item.title} free` },
}))
const topNames = platforms.slice(0, 3).map((p) => p.site)

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'Can you read manhwa for free legally?',
    a: `Yes. ${num(everyFree.length)} of the manhwa on manhwaindex have at least one official platform that gives part or all of the story away, usually with adverts or a wait between chapters. ${listWords(topNames)} carry the most of the popular ones.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Which app has the most free manhwa?',
    a: `Among the ${rows.length} most popular manhwa with a free option, ${platforms[0]?.site} carries ${platforms[0]?.count}, then ${platforms[1]?.site} with ${platforms[1]?.count} and ${platforms[2]?.site} with ${platforms[2]?.count}.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Is everything free on these apps?',
    a: 'Rarely. Most free platforms give away the older chapters and charge for the newest, or unlock one chapter at a time on a timer. Each title page says how the free part works on each platform.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Are these apps available in English?',
    a: `Not all of them. ${num(englishFree)} of the free titles have a free platform in English. Platforms shown with a language in brackets carry that title only in that language.`,
  },
]
---

<DataGuide
  slug={slug}
  title={meta.title}
  description={meta.description}
  category={meta.category}
  keywords={['free manhwa apps', 'read manhwa free legally', 'free manhwa', 'where to read manhwa for free', 'free webtoon apps']}
  hero={hero}
  items={rows.map(({ item }) => ({ name: item.title, path: pathOfTitle(item), image: item.cover }))}
  faq={faq}
  minutes={5}
>
  <p>
    You do not need a pirate site to read manhwa for free. The official apps that publish Korean comics
    give a lot of them away, paid for by adverts, by a wait between chapters, or by charging only for the
    newest episodes. Of the {num(withLinks)} manhwa on manhwaindex with an official platform,
    <strong>{num(everyFree.length)}</strong> ({percent(everyFree.length, withLinks)}) can be started free on at
    least one of them.
  </p>
  <p>
    Below are the {rows.length} most popular of those, with the free platforms named for each, so you can
    open the one that works where you live. {top && <>The most popular right now is <a href={pathOfTitle(top)}>{top.title}</a>.</>}
  </p>

  <h2>How this list is made</h2>
  <p>
    Every manhwa on this site carries the official platforms that publish it. A platform counts as free when its own model lets you read part of the story without
    paying: all of it, all but the newest chapters, the first chapters, or one chapter on a timer. A platform
    that only offers a trial, or nothing free at all, does not count, and neither does one we hold no facts for.
    This is the same rule as the "read free" page of each title. The list is then sorted by popularity on
    AniList, and titles kept off our homepage for adult content are left out.
  </p>

  <h2>The free platforms in this list</h2>
  <p>How many of the {rows.length} titles below each platform carries free, and how its free part works.</p>
  <table class="dg-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Platform</th>
        <th scope="col" class="n">Titles</th>
        <th scope="col">Free part</th>
        <th scope="col">After that</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {
        platforms.map((p) => {
          const facts = factsFor(p.site)
          const hub = hubSlugOf(p.site)
          return (
            <tr>
              <td>{hub ? <a href={`/platform/${hub}`}>{p.site}</a> : p.site}</td>
              <td class="n">{p.count}</td>
              <td>{facts.free || 'Not known'}</td>
              <td>{facts.pay || 'Not known'}</td>
            </tr>
          )
        })
      }
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>The {rows.length} most popular free manhwa</h2>
  <p>
    English platforms are listed first. A language in brackets means that platform carries the title only in
    that language.
  </p>
  <DataList rows={list} label="The most popular manhwa with a free official option" platformsLabel="Free on" />

  <h2>What "free" means on each app</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>WEBTOON</strong> and <strong>Tapas</strong> are the easiest start for English readers: most chapters
    are free, and only the newest ones cost coins or a wait. <strong>KakaoPage</strong>,
    <strong>Kakao Webtoon</strong> and <strong>Piccoma</strong> use a timer: one chapter unlocks every few hours
    if you are willing to wait. <strong>Tappytoon</strong> and <strong>Lezhin</strong> give away the opening
    chapters and sell the rest. Korean-language apps such as <strong>Naver Webtoon</strong> and
    <strong>Naver Series</strong> are free in the same ways, but only in Korean.
  </p>
  <p>
    Free chapters change all the time: a platform may lock older chapters, run a free-to-read event, or drop a
    title when its licence ends. If something here no longer matches what you see, the title's own page lists
    every official platform, free or not, and says how each one charges.
  </p>
</DataGuide>
